                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238466798",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198139127613",
                            "num_reviews": 438,
                            "playtime_forever": 478,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 478,
                            "last_played": 1792856941
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Now that it's almost Halloween, games like this one seem to be a good fit for a spooky time. Yomawari perfectly shows classic Japanese horror elements throughout the game. Looking out for our missing friend, we venture out and start looking to find her. Sounds easy; I mean, how hard can it be to find another kid that we know well? Sadly, it isn't so easy, and our path seems to be full of spirits that would attack at any given chance. This makes it hard and shows the bravery of the character we play as. I would absolutely lock myself in and wait until the adults step in to find her. If you're looking for a good time with horror elements, the game might be a good fit. If not, step away and hide under your blanket.",
